---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer — Calculator Street"
  description="Calculator Street calculators provide estimates based on entered measurements and assumptions. Verify project quantities, product data and safety-critical requirements."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
  dateModified="2026-09-24"
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Disclaimer" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] pt-6">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-mute">Last updated: September 24, 2026</p>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-6 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Estimates only</h2>
        <p>Calculator outputs are estimates based on the measurements, units and assumptions entered. Material density, package coverage, product yield, waste, pricing and site conditions vary. Confirm purchase quantities and current product specifications with the supplier before ordering.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Not professional advice</h2>
        <p>Nothing on this site is a substitute for professional construction, engineering, architectural or code advice. Structural and safety-critical decisions — including member sizing, load capacity, foundations, retaining walls, roofing assemblies and code compliance — should be checked against project documents, applicable requirements and qualified professional guidance.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Accuracy and assumptions</h2>
        <p>Calculator pages document the formula, worked example, assumptions and source links used for that tool. Even when the arithmetic is correct, real projects can differ because of irregular geometry, compaction, moisture, installation loss, product variation and measurement error. No calculator result is guaranteed to match field consumption or final project cost.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Material allowance</h2>
        <p>Where a calculator includes a material or waste allowance, choose a percentage appropriate for the actual project, product and installation method. The site does not treat one fixed allowance as universally correct.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">External sources</h2>
        <p>Individual calculator pages may cite manufacturer documentation, industry organizations, government references or other technical sources. Third-party content can change. Verify current specifications for the exact product and project.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Advertising and third-party services</h2>
        <p>Advertising or analytics services do not determine calculator results. Calculator arithmetic runs from the inputs and formulas implemented on the page. See the <a href="/privacy/" class="text-link underline">Privacy Policy</a> for information about cookies, consent and third-party services.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p>Found a possible error? Email <a href="mailto:hello@calculatorst.com" class="text-link underline">hello@calculatorst.com</a> with the calculator URL, inputs, expected result and supporting source if available.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
